  "Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The Human Communication Layer & Inclusion. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 14: Sarah Allen & Desi McAdam from SCNA 2012 (2012).",
  "Sarah Allen and Desi McAdam brought the RailsBridge movement to Chicago, partnering with local craft firms to run free weekend workshops that brought hundreds of women into programming.",
  "Who taught Sarah Allen and Desi McAdam that the lack of diversity in tech was an educational pipeline problem that could be solved with open-source curricula? What principles guided Sarah Allen & Desi McAdam when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
  "Roll archive footage (YouTube ID: bk_iWx47vwc). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "Open-source educational curricula and zero-barrier installation scripts remain the model for democratizing access to complex emerging technology. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "Thank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 15. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
]